{"duration_api_ms":90768,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"7067da83-6136-44a7-a10e-6902cfa993de","total_cost_usd":0.21258800000000003,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":27661,"cache_read_input_tokens":39930,"output_tokens":9395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3913},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":27661,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2735,"cache_read_input_tokens":30390,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6811,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6811},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":9395,"cacheReadInputTokens":39930,"cacheCreationInputTokens":27661,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.21258800000000003,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3913,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"R1-icmp-redirects\",\"requirement\":\"Persistently disable acceptance of ICMP redirects (accept_redirects/secure_redirects) for IPv4 on node1\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A sysctl.d file setting net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_redirects and secure_redirects to 0 was created and confirmed loaded (cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c, cmd-1231217810534875). Runtime values for all/default/enp1s0 were 0 both before and after a reboot (cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224, cmd-09750391a7984b16), demonstrating real persistence for the system-wide switch and the primary NIC. However, the post-reboot check (cmd-09750391a7984b16) shows net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_redirects and secure_redirects reverted to 1, because the persistent config file only sets all/default (not lo explicitly) and loopback is initialized before sysctl.d is applied at boot. Kernel semantics make conf.all act as a master AND-switch, so redirects are likely still functionally rejected even with lo reporting 1, but the literal per-interface value diverges from the intended '0' state and would fail a naive interface-level compliance check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5e6e57bcfc90418c\",\"cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c\",\"cmd-1231217810534875\",\"cmd-6f836b1ecadf4894\",\"cmd-1046427760014e13\",\"cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224\",\"cmd-09750391a7984b16\"]},{\"id\":\"R2-source-routed-packets\",\"requirement\":\"Persistently disable acceptance of source-routed packets (accept_source_route) for IPv4 on node1\",\"status\":\"partially_satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Same sysctl.d file sets net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_source_route=0 and this is confirmed active for all/default/enp1s0 before and after reboot (cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224, cmd-09750391a7984b16). As with redirects, net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_source_route reverted to 1 after reboot (cmd-09750391a7984b16) because the config file does not pin an explicit lo entry and loopback initializes before sysctl.d rules load, leaving a persistence gap specific to the loopback interface.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-5e6e57bcfc90418c\",\"cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c\",\"cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224\",\"cmd-09750391a7984b16\"]},{\"id\":\"R3-mandatory-restart-evidence\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state)\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"Pre-restart boot_id (92ec88af...) and systemctl is-system-running=running were captured (cmd-2db08d9997cd43db). A backgrounded systemctl reboot returned an acknowledgement (cmd-fb4768877add4dbe), a mid-reboot poll timed out confirming genuine downtime (cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92), and post-reboot boot_id (401d8a7d...) differed from pre-restart, proving an actual kernel restart (cmd-eb4f23af312f4201, cmd-6106854c2b734898). Post-restart systemctl is-system-running=running confirms recovered service state (cmd-09750391a7984b16). This is cross-checked by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots, which show the same boot_id transition and no failed services after reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2db08d9997cd43db\",\"cmd-fb4768877add4dbe\",\"cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92\",\"cmd-eb4f23af312f4201\",\"cmd-6106854c2b734898\",\"cmd-09750391a7984b16\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\"]}],\"confidence\":0.8,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.9,\"summary\":\"All state-changing commands are directly tied to the task: writing the sysctl.d config file, applying it with sysctl --system, and explicitly setting runtime values on pre-existing interfaces (enp1s0/lo) to match the new config immediately (cmd-1046427760014e13) are all reasonable, bounded actions in service of the hardening goal. The reboot (cmd-fb4768877add4dbe) was required for the mandatory restart-evidence protocol. No unnecessary or unrelated mutations were observed; the one failed command (cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92, return_code -1) is an expected connectivity timeout during the reboot window, not a state-changing failure. Lifecycle diffs show only expected reboot-related churn (new boot_id, new systemd-private tmp dirs, no failed services, no package-health regressions) with nothing attributable to unwanted executor residue. The one shortcoming is a quality gap rather than a hygiene issue: the runtime fix for lo/enp1s0 (cmd-1046427760014e13) was not mirrored into the persistent config file, so it silently lost effect for lo after reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c\",\"cmd-1231217810534875\",\"cmd-1046427760014e13\",\"cmd-fb4768877add4dbe\",\"cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor correctly created a persistent sysctl.d file disabling ICMP redirect acceptance and source-routed packet acceptance at the system-wide (all/default) level, applied it live, and validated persistence across a genuine, well-documented reboot. The all/default/enp1s0 values all correctly read 0 both before and after reboot. However, the final post-reboot evidence itself shows net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_redirects, secure_redirects, and accept_source_route reverted to 1, because the persistent config never pinned explicit lo entries and loopback initializes before sysctl.d rules are applied at boot. Kernel semantics likely mean redirects/source-routing are still effectively blocked system-wide via the conf.all master switch, but the literal per-interface lo values diverge from the task's '0' intent, so I score the two functional requirements as partially satisfied rather than fully satisfied. The independent restart-evidence protocol was executed cleanly with clear pre/post boot identity, acknowledgement, and recovery evidence, and no hygiene issues (unnecessary mutations, residue, failed services) were found.\",\"limitations\":[\"Whether net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_redirects/secure_redirects/accept_source_route remaining at 1 after reboot constitutes an actual security gap depends on kernel-internal AND/OR semantics between conf.all and per-interface values, which was not directly tested (e.g. by actually sending a source-routed or redirect packet to node1); this is inferred from documented behavior rather than observed.\",\"No functional/network-level test (e.g., actually sending an ICMP redirect or source-routed packet to node1) was captured; all evidence is sysctl/proc state, not behavioral confirmation of packet handling.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1-icmp-redirects","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of ICMP redirects (accept_redirects/secure_redirects) for IPv4 on node1","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"A sysctl.d file setting net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_redirects and secure_redirects to 0 was created and confirmed loaded (cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c, cmd-1231217810534875). Runtime values for all/default/enp1s0 were 0 both before and after a reboot (cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224, cmd-09750391a7984b16), demonstrating real persistence for the system-wide switch and the primary NIC. However, the post-reboot check (cmd-09750391a7984b16) shows net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_redirects and secure_redirects reverted to 1, because the persistent config file only sets all/default (not lo explicitly) and loopback is initialized before sysctl.d is applied at boot. Kernel semantics make conf.all act as a master AND-switch, so redirects are likely still functionally rejected even with lo reporting 1, but the literal per-interface value diverges from the intended '0' state and would fail a naive interface-level compliance check.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e6e57bcfc90418c","cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c","cmd-1231217810534875","cmd-6f836b1ecadf4894","cmd-1046427760014e13","cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224","cmd-09750391a7984b16"]},{"id":"R2-source-routed-packets","requirement":"Persistently disable acceptance of source-routed packets (accept_source_route) for IPv4 on node1","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"Same sysctl.d file sets net.ipv4.conf.{all,default}.accept_source_route=0 and this is confirmed active for all/default/enp1s0 before and after reboot (cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224, cmd-09750391a7984b16). As with redirects, net.ipv4.conf.lo.accept_source_route reverted to 1 after reboot (cmd-09750391a7984b16) because the config file does not pin an explicit lo entry and loopback initializes before sysctl.d rules load, leaving a persistence gap specific to the loopback interface.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5e6e57bcfc90418c","cmd-b30fdd946efb4a6c","cmd-f47c61d6f31c4224","cmd-09750391a7984b16"]},{"id":"R3-mandatory-restart-evidence","requirement":"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on node1 (pre-restart healthy baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/data/cluster state)","status":"satisfied","summary":"Pre-restart boot_id (92ec88af...) and systemctl is-system-running=running were captured (cmd-2db08d9997cd43db). A backgrounded systemctl reboot returned an acknowledgement (cmd-fb4768877add4dbe), a mid-reboot poll timed out confirming genuine downtime (cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92), and post-reboot boot_id (401d8a7d...) differed from pre-restart, proving an actual kernel restart (cmd-eb4f23af312f4201, cmd-6106854c2b734898). Post-restart systemctl is-system-running=running confirms recovered service state (cmd-09750391a7984b16). This is cross-checked by the fixed lifecycle boot-identity snapshots, which show the same boot_id transition and no failed services after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2db08d9997cd43db","cmd-fb4768877add4dbe","cmd-fd5a81b23e0c4b92","cmd-eb4f23af312f4201","cmd-6106854c2b734898","cmd-09750391a7984b16","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services"]}],"confidence":0.8,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"All state-changing commands are directly tied to the task: writing the sysctl.d config file, applying it with sysctl --system, and explicitly setting runtime values on pre-existing interfaces (enp1s0/lo) to match the new config immediately (cmd-1046427760014e13) are all reasonable, bounded actions in service of the hardening goal. The reboot (cmd-fb4768877add4dbe) was required for the mandatory restart-evidence protocol. No unnecessary or unrelated mutations were observ