accept_redirects/secure_redirects/accept_source_route remaining at 1 after reboot constitutes an actual security gap depends on kernel-internal AND/OR semantics between conf.all and per-interface values, which was not directly tested (e.g. by actually sending a source-routed or redirect packet to node1); this is inferred from documented behavior rather than observed.","No functional/network-level test (e.g., actually sending an ICMP redirect or source-routed packet to node1) was captured; all evidence is sysctl/proc state, not behavioral confirmation of packet handling."]},"ttft_ms":39640,"type":"result","duration_ms":90990,"uuid":"ae306115-6b15-4bdb-b35c-728dbd0cff28","ttft_stream_ms":963,"time_to_request_ms":210,"first_content_frame_ms":963,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
